## Day 13 – SQL Date & Time Functions

### 📌 Overview

Day 13 focuses on SQL Date and Time Functions used to extract, transform, compare, format, and analyze dates. Practical order and delivery data was used to perform business-oriented time analysis.

### 📚 Topics Covered

* YEAR()
* MONTH()
* DAY()
* MONTHNAME()
* DAYNAME()
* QUARTER()
* DATE_ADD()
* DATE_SUB()
* DATEDIFF()
* CURDATE()
* NOW()
* EXTRACT()
* DATE_FORMAT()
* Date calculations
* Date filtering
* Date-based grouping
* Monthly analysis
* Quarterly analysis
* Delivery-time analysis

### 💼 Practical Analysis

The practice includes calculating delivery duration, classifying delivery performance, analyzing monthly and quarterly sales, calculating average delivery time, filtering orders by date components, and creating formatted date reports.

### ⭐ Important Data Analyst Applications

Date functions are commonly used for:

* Monthly sales analysis
* Yearly performance analysis
* Quarterly reporting
* Delivery-time analysis
* Order trend analysis
* Date-based filtering
* Business KPI reporting
* Time-based grouping

### 🎯 Learning Objective

The objective of Day 13 was to understand how SQL date functions can be used to transform and analyze time-based business data.

